 "sentences": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "text": "This man is about to die, so someone sent for the bird.",
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 2.9
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "text": "In the 1600s, when plague hit a town, the doctor showed up dressed like a nightmare.",
   "s": 3.2,
   "e": 8.78
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "text": "Black robe, black hat, and a long curved beak over his whole face.",
   "s": 9.18,
   "e": 12.78
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "text": "It wasn't a costume. It was a gas mask, four hundred years early.",
   "s": 13.18,
   "e": 16.9
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "text": "You see, doctors believed plague travelled through the air as a poison fog they called miasma.",
   "s": 17.14,
   "e": 22.58
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "text": "Bad air, bad smells, dead people. To them, it was the same thing.",
   "s": 22.84,
   "e": 26.58
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "text": "So the beak was stuffed with roses, mint, and camphor.",
   "s": 26.8,
   "e": 29.56
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "text": "Every breath he took got filtered through flowers.",
   "s": 29.76,
   "e": 32.14
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "text": "The robe was leather, rubbed with wax, sealing him from head to toe.",
   "s": 32.54,
   "e": 36.16
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "text": "He carried a long stick, so he could examine patients and lift their clothes without ever touching them.",
   "s": 36.4,
   "e": 42.02
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "text": "And the strangest part? It kind of worked.",
   "s": 42.2,
   "e": 44.38
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "text": "Not because of the herbs. Herbs did nothing.",
   "s": 44.58,
   "e": 46.9
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "text": "But a waxed coat and a beak meant the real killers, flea bites, couldn't reach his skin.",
   "s": 47.12,
   "e": 51.84
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "text": "Plague doctors kept dying anyway. Most of them never stood a chance.",
   "s": 52.08,
   "e": 55.84
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "text": "But the ones who sealed up tight and kept their distance lived a little longer.",
   "s": 56.3,
   "e": 60.12
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "text": "They were fighting the wrong enemy, with almost the right suit.",
   "s": 60.34,
   "e": 63.24
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "text": "Four hundred years ago, that was as close to a hazmat suit as you could get.",
   "s": 63.52,
   "e": 67.64
  }
 ]
}